{
  "version": 1,
  "source": "seed",
  "entity": "occasion_country",
  "origin": "authored",
  "notes": [
    "plan/13 D6: every rule below is transcribed from plan/03 §9's rule types and must be verified against an official calendar for the destination before that country's status flips to `live`. plan/09 line 3's five reference dates are pinned by tests/unit/seed-dataset.test.ts as rules, not as computed dates: the evaluator `occasionDate(rule, year)` is spec 009's.",
    "Rows cover the seven destination countries of src/config/countries.ts and the eighteen seasonal occasions of plan/10 §1.1. Evergreen occasions carry no row: occasion_country exists to hold a per-destination date, and an evergreen occasion has none in any country.",
    "`observed: false` with the `none` rule is a deliberate value, not a gap: it says the destination does not keep the occasion, which is what stops a country occasion page from existing for it (plan/02 §6, ADR-0007). konfirmation, student, omatag and 17_mai are market-specific to countries we do not deliver to yet and are unobserved everywhere.",
    "One observed occasion carries the `none` rule because it has no computable date: PL `name_day` (imieniny) is per name, so the occasion is a category rather than a dated event (plan/13 B15, spec 009 AC-12 — unchanged).",
    "RO `easter` carried the `none` rule until spec 009 AC-12 (TASK-122) added the seventh rule type. It now reads `orthodox_easter_offset(0)`: the Julian computus read on the Gregorian calendar. The 2026–2030 dates it produces — 12 Apr 2026, 2 May 2027, 16 Apr 2028, 8 Apr 2029, 28 Apr 2030 — were verified against the official calendar of the Romanian Patriarchate (calendar.patriarhia.ro, retrieved 2026-09-18, which publishes 2026 and gives 12 Apr 2026 as Învierea Domnului) and against two independent tables of the Julian computus; the verification and its sources are in the header of tests/fixtures/occasions.ts.",
    "PL `grandparents_day` carries Dzień Babci (21 January); Dzień Dziadka (22 January) shares the same campaign window and would need a second occasion key to be its own row.",
    "`promoStartOffsetDays` is the number of days before the date that the campaign window opens: 21 for Christmas, 14 for Valentine's, Mother's Day, Easter and All Saints, 7 for the rest, 0 where there is no date."
  ],
